{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdPYgvYboXQyg8jZbkSUv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BzxLxLktFZgXCb6aJwsmwa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/arena-ws.JO3Txm/SOLUTION.md","content":"# SOLUTION\n\nTwo bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`, both in the recency bookkeeping:\n\n1. **`get` did not count as a \"use\".** It read the entry out of the\n   `OrderedDict` but never moved it to the end, so the LRU ordering only ever\n   reflected insertion order. A key that had just been read was still treated as\n   least-recently-used and got evicted on the next `put`. Fixed by calling\n   `move_to_end(key)` on a successful (non-expired) lookup.\n\n2. **`put` evicted on every call once full, even when updating an existing\n   key.** The capacity check ran before checking membership, so overwriting a\n   key already in the cache dropped an unrelated entry and left the cache one\n   item under capacity. Fixed by only evicting when the key is genuinely new\n   (`key not in self._data`).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":223,"cache_read_input_tokens":22646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":223,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a1dc45a-fbc9-47a1-a1b8-282cf2ea11cd","uuid":"4aba28aa-8e52-4027-85af-5e806349b73c","timestamp":"2026-07-25T22:15:12.886Z","request_id":"req_011CdPYgumiWLRhN4SRMgEry"}
